`cmd` directory defines entrypoint for starting a http server.

`docs` directory contains file `schema.txt` that documents (when last refreshed) the whole schema of the postgres databse.

postgres sql migration files are located in `migrate` directory

Go style: [docs/go.md](docs/go.md). Filenames: all lowercase, no hyphens or underscores, one word when possible (`get.go`, `admin.go`, `types.go`).

For context:
- "tester" is hosted in a seperate code repo. "tester" to AWS SQS for code execution jobs and streams back results
- "website" is also a seperate repository that hosts next.js website code